    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0624" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2385: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-22T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 22,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your August 26, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>Please ascertain and advise the Department as precisely as possible what powers
                    have been entrusted to Hsu En Yuan. It is particularly desired to know whether
                    he is authorized to renew the existing Chicago Bank loan of $5,000,000<anchor
                        n="17" xml:id="d478-f1"/> and whether he is empowered to negotiate for the
                    supplementary loan of $25,000,000 contemplated by the contract.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
